      <h2>Lush doesn't have to mean thirsty</h2>
      <p class="lead">A water-wise yard isn't gravel and cactus. Done well, it's some of the most layered, alive-looking design there is — it just happens to survive a Hill Country August and stay comfortably inside Hays County watering restrictions.</p>
      <p>We build around native and adapted plants that evolved for Central Texas soil and heat, group them by how much water they actually want, and prep the clay-and-caliche ground so water soaks in where roots can reach it. The result is a landscape that looks intentional, needs far less from you, and keeps its beauty when the next drought hits.</p>
